note right of channel_crypto.channel_crypto
  E2E encryption Phase 2 (issue
  #138). MainWindow orchestrates:
  creating an encrypted channel
  generates a key here, wraps it
  for the creator's own identity
  (IdentityKeyStore) immediately,
  then for every other community
  member once listMembers()/
  fetchProfile() resolve their
  public key. Opening an encrypted
  channel fetches+unwraps this
  login's own wrapped copy first
  (fetchMyChannelKey()) before
  subscribing/loading history —
  myChannelKeyNotFound() means no
  one has granted this login access
  yet. Resolved keys are cached in
  MainWindow's channelKeys_ for the
  session only, never persisted.

  encryptMessage()/decryptMessage()
  wrap chat-service's existing
  {"body"} field — chat-service
  itself never changes, it just
  relays/stores a longer opaque
  string. Attachments and server
  search stay unavailable for an
  encrypted channel this phase
  (ChatView disables both buttons;
  chat-service also rejects with
  400 as a second line of defense).
end note

note right of ChatClient
  Async only — every call returns
  immediately, result comes back
  via signals. First frame after
  connecting authenticates and
  subscribes to a channel; every
  frame after that is a chat message.
end note

note right of ChatRestClient
  Separate from ChatClient on purpose:
  CRUD/management (this class) vs. the
  live message stream (ChatClient) are
  different responsibilities.
end note

